,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm approving PKT-0106. It was a measure-and-diagnose round, and it did what it set out to do.\n\n**Goal**\n- **Measurements:** the round 2 numbers are in `.theseus/oracle/rounds/web-apps-documenteditor-r2.md`. They cover both oracles and 5 runs of `perf/open-window.js`, timed when the editor asks for the document (LoadDoc) and when the document is ready. Busy time before LoadDoc is split by source: vendor files, documenteditor's own code, apps/common, script parse and compile, and sdkjs.\n- **Diagnosis:** `.theseus/diagnosis/DIAG-web-apps-documenteditor.md` was replaced, with the required header: `round: 2`, `goals_hash: dcb03039`, and the executor's model id in `diagnosed_by`.\n- **What round 1 delivered:** the diagnosis says it plainly. Round 1 produced measurements and oracles but no speed gain.\n- **The verdict follows from the evidence:** round 1's condition was over 200 ms of this module's time before LoadDoc. Both rounds measured about 0.9 s.\n- **The next-round plan** is in machine-readable form. Each step is a JavaScript change in `external/web-apps`, must pass both oracles, and needs a 5-run before/after. It also says when to give up: if P1 and P2 together gain less than 150 ms, the verdict becomes keep, and if an earlier LoadDoc doesn't make the document ready sooner, the work moves to sdkjs.\n- **No `-b` file:** there was none, and the log says so.\n\n**Contract**\n- No source code changed. The web-apps fork has no diff against its base, and the main repo diff touches only `.theseus` files.\n\n**Budget**\n- 4 files and about 140 diff lines, against limits of 6 files and 1,500 lines.\n\n**Rejection rules (TEP-0004)**\n- The executor log is filled in.\n- No follow-up packets were requested. The next-round work comes from the plan in the diagnosis, not from spawn requests.\n- This is an investigate packet, not a characterize one, so no surprise had to be kept in a test.\n- The \"reject when there is no measured gain\" rule is for packets meant to make things faster. This packet was forbidden to change code, so it doesn't apply. The differential being pure noise (the same commit on both sides) is the expected result, and the packet records it.\n\n**Small points for the next round, not blocking**\n- **Lessons not saved:** the \"Lessons for the Atlas\" section of the packet is empty. The two lessons appear only in the executor's report and should be added to the packet and the Atlas.\n- **Plan ordering:** P2 depends on P1, yet both are in wave 0. P1 and P2 touch different files, so P2 could drop that dependency, or move to wave 1.\n- **Two sets of timings:** the differential numbers in the round 2 file come from a different run than the factory's output. Both show the same ±0.7 s noise, which supports the plan's rule that a gain only counts over repeated runs.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE round 2 diagnosis is complete, evidence-backed, within contract and budget; next-round plan has measurable gates","ttft_ms":5317,"type":"result","duration_ms":27705,"uuid":"02db83ed-e9b7-454b-857f-4b3b90621b98","ttft_stream_ms":4469,"time_to_request_ms":398,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":8,"system_prompt":254,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":22,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":14,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":31,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":3,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":48,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":259,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":210,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":138,"process_rss_mib_result":209,"process_anon_mib_result":124,"process_peak_rss_mib":217,"process_cpu_ms_turn":11